:4,"h":"grapevine","note":"missed a Surrey cross-country vest in 1951; selected for Surrey in the Inter-Counties 10 miles road walk 25 years later"},{"id":"B192-20","when":"August 1976","p":11},{"id":"B192-25","when":"August 1976","p":13},{"id":"B192-28","when":"August 1976","p":15,"h":"JUNE 12th 1976 - VAUXHALL MOTORS 10km."},{"id":"B192-79","when":"August 1976","p":32,"h":"SPOTLIGHT on JOHN BROMLEY","note":"born Patricroft, Manchester, 9.2.28; joined Army 1942 aged 14; won Army College 1 mile Championship 1943; joined Belgrave 1949; turned to race walking; chosen for Surrey in Inter-Counties 10 miles Road Walking Championship 1976; titles include Welsh Youths A.A.A. 1 mile 1944, Singapore A.A.A. 880y and 1 mile 1947, Surrey County A.A.A. and Army A.A. 2 mile steeplechase records 1953, Belgrave Club 880y and 1 mile 1954; coached in Kenya; achilles ruptured in Kenya; took up race walking at the Police Cadet School in 1970; won Singapore to Jahore Bahru 17.5 miles walk 1955; won Club Championships 880 yards (1:59.6) and 1 mile (4:24.8) 1954; Physical Training Officer at Hendon Cadet School; qualified A.A.A. coach in every event; former Army Senior Athletic Coach; team manager and coach to British Modern Pentathlon 'B' teams 1968"},{"id":"B192-98","when":"August 1976","p":42,"h":"Blackheath H ~ Philips 100 x 1mile","note":"leg 25, 5:39"},{"id":"B193-33","when":"December 1976","p":16,"h":"OCTOBER 2nd 1976 - WIMBLEDON.","note":"12th 44:55"},{"id":"B193-39","when":"December 1976","p":20,"h":"WALKING '76","note":"1976 bests: 3Km 16:11, 10Km 55:58"},{"id":"B194-104","when":"April 1977","p":55,"h":"MARCH 19th 1977 - COVENTRY - R.W.A. 10 MILES CHAMPIONSHIP ~ SENT TO COVENTRY!"},{"id":"B194-81","when":"April 1977","p":48,"h":"WALKING","note":"walker; first man home as Belgrave won the Garnet for the first time since '68; fourth man in winning G.L.C. team"},{"id":"B194-83","when":"April 1977","p":49,"h":"NOVEMBER 6th 1976 - IMBER COURT - CIVIL SERVICE '7' ~ Another 'PB' from J